<section>
  <section>
    <h1>Testing with the keyboard</h1>
  </section>
  <section class="compact">
    <p>
      Open the webpage and only use the TAB key to navigate through it, don't
      use the mouse or trackpad.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Can you reach each interactive element with TAB? (WCAG 2.1.1)</li>
      <li>Are non interactive elements not reachable with TAB?</li>
      <li>Is the focus visible for each element? (WCAG 2.4.7)</li>
      <li>Is the TAB order logical? (WCAG 2.4.3)</li>
      <li>Are there no keyboard traps? (WCAG 2.1.2)</li>
      <li>
        Can each interactive element be activated with the keyboard (usually
        ENTER, SPACE or arrow)? (WCAG 2.1.1)
      </li>
      <li>Is focus managed properly? (WCAG 2.4.3)</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>Skip links</h3>
    <p>Not mandatory but should be implemented properly if present</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Is the skip link the first link of the page?</li>
      <li>Does it become visible when it has focus?</li>
      <li>
        Is the link text meaningful and in same language as page (for example
        "go to main content")?
      </li>
      <li>
        Does it work? When pressing ENTER, is focus moved to main content? Is
        next TAB stop in the main content?
      </li>
      <li>Are there not too many skip links?</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Focus management</h2>
    <p>Sometimes when new content appears on the page, focus should move</p>
    <ul>
      <li>When a new page is loaded, focus should go to top of new page</li>
      <li>
        When{' '}
        <a
          target="tweede"
          href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/dialog-modal/">
          modal dialog
        </a>{' '}
        opens, focus should go to dialog window
      </li>
      <li>
        After pressing the submit button on a form, focus is expected to move
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Focus management</h2>
    <p>Sometimes focus should not move:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        When using a button to expand or collapse content (){' '}
        <a
          target="tweede"
          href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/disclosure/">
          disclosure
        </a>{' '}
        or{' '}
        <a
          target="tweede"
          href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/accordion/">
          accordion
        </a>
        )
      </li>
      <li>
        When selecting a TAB in a{' '}
        <a
          target="tweede"
          href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/tabs/">
          tablist
        </a>
        , focus should stay on the TAB
      </li>
      <li>
        When using a dynamic filter, focus should stay on filter (checkbox,
        button, ...)
      </li>
      <li>When interacting with form fields (checkbox, edit, select,...)</li>
      <li>See design patterns in case of doubt</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</section>
